# No planning tags in durable text

Planning docs (`_planning/`, design notes, chat) may use short slice/item tags
such as `S1`, `S2a`, `H3`, `F5`, `M1` when discussing work breakdown.

**Do not** put those tags in places that persist in the product history:

- Git commit messages
- Code comments and `@file` / `@brief` Doxygen text
- Public headers, READMEs meant as product docs, or user-facing strings

Prefer plain language instead (e.g. "hub attachment RAII guard", "control owns
channel", "DataPlane variant handle").

Tags remain fine inside `_planning/` notes and ephemeral chat.
